id.instance: String (TS "c<n>")
num.game: i32
num.cursor: u32
map.ordered: IndexMap
bag.data: IndexMap<String, serde_json::Value>
error.style: Result<_, EngineError> with TS's message; panic only on invariants
null.optional: Option + skip_serializing_if
null.nullable: Option, serialised null
case.json: camelCase via serde rename_all
case.rust: snake_case
state.mut: &mut GameState writes, &GameState reads, &mut EngineSink for TS sink mutators
rng.source: Rng::new(&state.seed, state.rng_cursor) and write the cursor back
hook.style: Arc<dyn Fn(&mut EffectContext) -> Vec<Effect> + Send + Sync> via hook(); no fn pointers, no Box
registry.style: OnceLock set once by register_all; fused scripts built on lookup from state; tests use the testkit's thread-local register_scripts over registered_scripts_now() (override if set, else production)
async.style: tokio in crates/server only; none in pure crates
log.style: tracing JSON to stdout, server only
test.live_objects: owned CardInstance copies; re-read with s.card(&copy), write with find_instance_mut
test.sink: local Rng from create_rng(seed, cursor) + local Vec<GameEvent> + EngineSink::new(s.state_mut(), ..); cursor not written back (as TS)
test.literals: scenario and effect args json!/json_as(json!); fixture CardDefs json_as(json!)
test.events: events_of(&PlayerView, GameEventType) -> Vec<GameEvent>; toEqual via serde JSON or PartialEq
test.register_all: jackioh_cards::register_all() at the start of every test
